WEBVTT

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.000
Huci's probably harvesting grain right now.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.000
The flocks of wild geese in the skies

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.110
are a sign that the salmon which bring 
us treasure are coming up the river.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.760
We call the salmon "Kamuycep,"
"the fish of the gods."

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.030
Or "sipe," "real food."

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.010
Sugimoto, get that for me.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.480
It's kutci. Kiwi berries.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.990
This kutci is great, Asirpa-san.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.360
It's so sweet.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.070
If you eat too much kutci, 
your anus starts to itch.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.030
So eat a lot, Sugimoto.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.370
The Ainu of the east call 
wild strawberries "salmon strawberries,"

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:13.090
because when they turn red, it's time 
for the salmon to come up the river.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.470
The Ainu look forward to 
the salmon every year, huh?

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:31.320
Look, Sugimoto. A bear made 
that with their claws.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.360
At this time of year,
bears eat nothing but kiwi berries,

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.500
so sometimes their meat
 will taste like kutci, too.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.950
You really know a lot, Asirpa-san.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.070
My aca taught me everything.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.950
About the mountains,

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.010
the Ainu... Everything.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.010
Sugimoto...

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:02.090
I'm scared.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.920
If the Nopperabo who killed the Ainu 
and stole their gold is my father...

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.310
What do I do then?

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.390
<b>Abashiri Prison</b>

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.290
Asirpa-san, we've come so far 
that you have to meet him.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.500
No matter what happens,
I'm with you until the end.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.090
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:21.000
<b>Episode Twenty-Two
On the Night of the New Moon</b>

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:24.990
Abashiri Prison is surrounded by mountains.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.780
There are several dozen 
posts with armed guards.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.910
It's particularly well-guarded 
on the sides with mountains,

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.750
because that's where the prisoners are kept.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.730
They're not just worried about escapes.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:39.210
They're worried about people 
coming to take Nopperabo.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.990
Which means we need to go through 
the wall on the Abashiri side,

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.510
where it's less well-guarded.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.130
Here.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.060
We can only pull this plan off now, 
while the salmon are spawning.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.400
We'll use an Ainu hut to 
hide the tunnel entrance.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:17.560
You can't build this here!

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.960
Somebody's here.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.090
Take this thing down!

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.420
You don't need to build it here, do you?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.620
So you want even more salmon?

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.560
What do you mean?

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:41.730
We made a deal. Three salmon a day in 
exchange for the right to fish here.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.030
Ask those guards.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.500
You guys were taking bribes?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.660
We want five.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.830
Or you take that down. Got it?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:02.150
We'd be better off letting 
the foxes get them!

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:06.420
Chief Kadokura, make sure 
you don't tell Warden Inudou.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.300
Of course, you idiot.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.950
Salmon used to be 
the Ainu's primary food source.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:33.470
<b>Huci's
13th
Younger
 Sister</b>

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.940
In years when there were very 
few salmon, people starved.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:39.420
That's why we use every part of the salmon.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.240
Chop off the head,

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:46.760
then cut out the cartilage, called "hizu,"
in the middle of the upper jaw.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.800
There's a dish you can make with it.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.190
Sugimoto, do you know what it is?

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:55.940
Don't tell me... No way!
Is it what I think it is?

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:56.860
Chitatap!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.810
Did you hear that? Chitatap!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.940
"Chitatap" originally just 
referred to the kind made from salmon.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.080
So it's the chitatap of all chitataps!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.320
Ow! Stop grabbing me!

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:10.110
You make chitatap from the gills and hizu.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.700
The more you mince it, the better it gets.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:14.070
Chitatap, chitatap, chitatap,
 chitatap, chitatap, chitatap...

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:17.160
Can I use this to make chitatap?

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:21.120
Chitatap. Chitatap. Chitatap.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.540
Ogata...

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.310
Everybody else is saying chitatap.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:30.040
If you're not willing to 
say it for real chitatap,

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.130
when will you say it?

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.180
I wanted everyone to come together.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:38.520
Chitatap.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.100
He said it!

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.060
Did you hear that? Ogata just said "chitatap"!

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.110
You didn't hear it?!

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.670
This is "chiporosayo," salmon roe in porridge.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:58.040
This is "cipor rataskep,"
crushed potatoes mixed with roe.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.400
It's soft and easy to chew!

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.460
So this is real "chitatap," huh?

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.220
We just caught the fish,
so it doesn't smell strong at all.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.300
Hinna, hinna!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.260
The skewered fish is nice and fatty, too.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:21.010
Inkarmat-san, was it?

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.600
You got a man?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.320
Hey!

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:33.630
Here.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.240
What are you doing, Cikapasi?

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:40.500
If a girl goes to boy's 
house and makes him a meal,

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.880
and he eats half of it and gives it back,

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.620
then she eats the rest,

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.250
that makes them betrothed.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.840
An Ainu proposal, basically?

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.090
Why not be a real family?

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.720
I like it! Hot!

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.550
Cikapasi, give that back.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:14.240
Oh, it was still delicate, huh?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.020
Tanigaki Nispa...

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.960
You were watching Abashiri Prison 
from the other side of the river.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:29.460
You say you don't think Nopperabo is Wilk.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:33.420
But you came all the way here because 
a part of you hopes he is, right?

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.050
You're right.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:43.870
I wandered alone as an orphan 
until I met him in Otaru.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.060
The time I spent with him was too beautiful.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:50.170
It still has a hold on me.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:55.480
But my fortune-telling said 
we'll never meet again.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:10:01.120
Every time another of my fortunes 
came true, my desire to see him only grew.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.200
And then I heard of his death.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:11.930
It was impossible. The reason I was never 
going to see him again was my own death.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.260
That's what my fortune-telling said.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.720
But when I looked into his death,

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.890
I met Lt. Tsurumi, who said 
he had his belongings.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:27.350
Wilk was dead. And the Nopperabo in the 
prison knew the location of the gold,

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.300
and was working with Kiroranke.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.280
That's what he said.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:38.200
For a while, I was satisfied that maybe 
my fortune-telling wasn't always right.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:43.830
But when I was drowning 
in the lake, I felt it.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.350
I truly was destined to die then.

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:52.710
But you changed the fate my 
fortune-telling laid out for me.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:57.080
Fate can be changed, I learned!

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:01.450
You may not understand this,

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:07.220
but for the moment, I have hope 
that I can see Wilk again.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:12.120
But it's not a desire to see someone I love.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.860
It's because I want to 
free myself from my past.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.220
I want to go into the future 
with you, Tanigaki Nispa!

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:31.790
I still have a job of my own... 
To bring Asirpa back to Huci.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:41.130
When the time comes, I'll give 
you that half-eaten bowl of food.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:48.910
He's eating Tanigaki Nispa's food!

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:55.980
<b>A few days later</b>

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.550
Hey, Kiroranke.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.480
Where does this come out? 
Is this really okay?

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:04.660
We dug the distance 
Hijikata Toshizou told us to.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.950
We have to believe him.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:10.920
I sure as hell hope we don't poke our 
heads out into the guards' tavern.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:19.530
Welcome.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:20.760
Just as planned.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.430
Where are we?

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.260
My lodgings.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:34.680
Warden Inudou's orders are that Nopperabo 
be moved to a different cell every day.

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:39.320
But I can tell you exactly 
where he'll be moved.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:44.430
On the night of the next full moon,
Nopperabo will be moved here,

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.200
to Cell #66 in Building 4.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.450
If we break in, get Asirpa-chan 
in front of Nopperabo,

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.750
and leave without a trace, we win.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:13:01.790
If we fail, they'll find the tunnel
and Kadokura will be a wanted man.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:05.310
If that happens, 
I'll follow you, Hijikata-san.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:10.980
Before he died, my father fought with 
you on the side of the old shogunate.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.770
He'd be happy to see me follow you.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:20.480
If Nopperabo is Asirpa-chan's father, 
will it be hard to get him out?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:24.740
He's had one of his Achilles tendons cut,
so it will be very hard,

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.950
but not impossible.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.420
There's no need to take 
the risk to get him out.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.160
If my father really is Nopperabo...

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:37.660
Stop hiding down there and come up.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.850
I've heard about you.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:49.510
Ogata Hyakunosuke is the son of the mistress 
of the former leader of the 7th Division.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:53.690
For somebody who just 
deserted to get the gold,

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.520
you have a complicated backstory.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:02.630
Like hell do I want to run the 7th. 
What a pain in the ass that would be.

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:07.470
Don't tell me you guys 
trust each other, either.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:17.870
Inkarmat-chan, have you ever used 
fortune-telling to see who Nopperabo is?

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:20.090
Many times.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.880
Many times!

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.890
It always comes back, "No."

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:29.380
In other words, he's not 
Asirpa-chan's father.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:33.010
But lately, there's been 
more and more yeses.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:36.000
Which side is winning now?

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.730
I just did it a while ago.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.900
Out of 1,000 tries, I just 
got the 500th "yes."

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:46.360
Then... will you do it one last time?

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:15.720
Shiraishi-san?

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.020
Never mind.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.170
We don't need the uncertainty.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:24.680
We just need to go find out for ourselves.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:33.080
<i>And finally, on a black, moonless night...</i>

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.910
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:40.720
Inkarmat, Cikapasi, Nagakura, and Ienaga,

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:41.950
you stay in the kotan.

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:44.180
Ogata, you hide in the mountains.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:46.220
Back us up with your rifle if we need it.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.680
Tanigaki, you stand by with the 
log rafts we hid by the riverside.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.880
Kiroranke, Ushiyama, Hijikata,

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.260
you stand by in the lodging house.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:16:00.430
Shiraishi, Asirpa-san, and myself will
 sneak inside Nopperabo's prison.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.380
The lights are off in the prison.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:07.400
We'll run right through the 
darkness and get close to it.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:10.360
Toni Anji will take the lead.

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:12.840
The sound of the wind is strong tonight,

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:15.820
but I can tell where I am in 
relation to the buildings.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:19.740
And it will hide the sound 
of my tongue clicking.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.710
Okay, let's go!

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:29.300
Who are you people?

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.790
They found us already!

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:39.230
Toni, do you have gunk in your ears?

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:41.370
How the hell did you miss them, moron?

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.410
You morons missed the lamp!

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.560
Shh!

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.440
We've got this! Go!

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:55.350
Starting tomorrow, Chief Kadokura's 
an unemployed and wanted man.

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:57.370
We're off to a bad start.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.070
This is it.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:12.940
<i>The Five Radial Wards of Abashiri Prison.</i>

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:14.420
<b>The Five Radial Wards of Abashiri Prison</b>

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.990
<i>They are capable of holding 
over 700 prisoners,</i>

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:19.540
<i>and at the center of the five 
wings is a central watchtower</i>

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:23.480
<i>that can see the whole area.</i>

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.470
All the windows have bars.

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:30.230
Except one.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:32.020
The one on the ceiling.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:35.170
It's the only way in.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.850
I can hear you!

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:13.370
Man, it sure is windy tonight.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:13.970
Yes.

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:14.640
Whoa!

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:18.150
Oh no, my cup... Ow!

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:19.320
Are you okay?

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.980
Did you cut yourself?

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:22.670
Don't worry, Chief Kadokura.

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:23.740
We'll clean it up for you.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.160
Thanks...

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.590
<b>Cell #66</b>

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:58.490
<i>Aca...</i>

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:02.710
Asirpa, come here.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.410
Ushiyama, where did Hijikata go?

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.910
He's not here?

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.060
There's something not 
right about that old man.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.070
Aca?

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:29.770
Aca... is that you?

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:32.280
It's me.

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.730
Asirpa.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.440
I came from Otaru to see you.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.900
Shiraishi. Match.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:58.880
No... that's not Aca!

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:01.130
Intruders!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.050
Kadokura!

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:08.910
Sugimoto!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:10.870
Asirpa-san!

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.520
Run, Asirpa-san!

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:18.230
Sugimoto!

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:23.190
Huh? My gun's not working!

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.910
Neither is mine!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.620
You must have never cleaned them!

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:32.640
Is this Kiroranke's buddy? The one 
Inkarmat-chan was talking about?

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:36.100
Enemy attack! Get the hell up!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.830
Are you with Kiroranke?

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:40.790
Well?!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.550
So he's a double.

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:46.660
Seriously? Would you go that far?

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.620
I don't know, but...

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.430
Somebody's set us up.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.270
<i>You guys need to stay here.</i>

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:59.630
Wait, Toni! Sugimoto is still...

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:03.280
Where are we going? 
The tunnel's the other way!

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.770
I'll bring you to the real one!

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.330
Warden Inudou!

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:15.790
Intruders in Ward 4!

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.750
They've finally come for Nopperabo?

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.000
This is not good!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.130
Get back here, now!

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.510
Inkarmat? What are you doing here?

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.140
Tanigaki Nispa, run.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.040
If you stay here, you'll get
 caught up in it, too.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.520
There they are! There they are!

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:49.820
I told them you'd send a telegram 
to Otaru under a false name.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:52.830
Inkarmat, what did you—

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.790
I'm seeing lights coming up Abashiri River!

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:59.250
They're almost to the bridge!

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.580
Calm down.

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:02.670
Just remember your training.

00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:10.220
The bridge!

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.980
They really attacked?

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:15.180
The 7th is here!

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:19.260
So they were watching us?

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:22.900
You shouldn't underestimate an 
intelligence officer, I guess.

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:25.830
That's the only bridge connecting 
us to the opposite shore!

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:28.250
It'll buy us time!

00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:30.370
Get ready to fight!

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:32.580
The bridge has been destroyed.

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:35.820
Yes! This is what I've been waiting for!

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:43.940
<b>Ikazuchi-class Destroyer</b>

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:59.190
<i>Rear Admiral Koito Heiji,
Commander of the Ominato Guard District...</i>

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:01.400
<i>Second Lieutenant Koito's father.</i>

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:02.360
Go.

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:09.300
We've passed the remains of the bridge!

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:11.640
We'd take fewer casualties

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:19.290
if we were just creepy creatures who feed 
on the orcas after they kill each other.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:22.710
No matter how well-armed they are, 
they're still just prison guards.

00:23:23.070 --> 00:23:26.670
Tonight, we're the hunting orcas!

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.040
Capture Nopperabo and Asirpa!

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Overwhelmed</b>

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:39.890
Next Time: "Overwhelmed."
